ource":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"2488af0f5162b903d92b46b56a071d779cc84c0988c43ab30214ea5cf25f16ff","quote":"An operating segment is a component of the Company that engages in business activities from which it may earn revenue and incur expenses and is identified on the basis of the internal financial reports that are provided to and regularly reviewed by the Company’s chief operating decision maker in order to allocate resources and assess performance of the segment.","context":"Segment Information","section":"Segment Information","block":1000,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"536d17ad8c4479c3526fb79403ee4eec9b069aa03470e7196e0505aae26b55ce","quote":"In accordance with ASC 280, Segment Reporting, operating segments are defined as components of an enterprise about which separate financial information is available that is evaluated regularly by the chief operating decision maker (the “CODM”) in deciding how to allocate resources and in assessing performance. The Company’s revenue segments have similar economic characteristics, and they are managed as a single business unit. The Company uses the “management approach” in determining reportable operating segments. The management approach considers the internal organization and reporting used by the Company’s CODM for making operating decisions and assessing performance as the source for determining the Company’s reportable segments. The Company’s CODM reviews results when making decisions about allocating resources and assessing performance of the Company. The Company has determined that there is only one reportable operating segment.","context":"An operating segment is a component of the Company that engages in business activities from which it may earn revenue and incur expenses and is identified on the basis of the internal financial reports that are provided to and regularly reviewed by the Company’s chief operating decision maker in order to allocate resources and assess performance of the segment.","section":"Segment Information","block":1001,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"c59259275348040be8379588ab9bffdfb0ba60f00ead9c1d66dd6abc4db95d55","quote":"F-16","context":"In accordance with ASC 280, Segment Reporting, operating segments are defined as components of an enterprise about which separate financial information is available that is evaluated regularly by the chief operating decision maker (the “CODM”) in deciding how to allocate resources and in assessing performance. The Company’s revenue segments have similar economic characteristics, and they are managed as a single business unit. The Company uses the “management approach” in determining reportable operating segments. The management approach considers the internal organization and reporting used by the Company’s CODM for making operating decisions and assessing performance as the source for determining the Company’s reportable segments. The Company’s CODM reviews results when making decisions about allocating resources and assessing performance of the Company. The Company has determined that there is only one reportable operating segment.","section":"Segment Information","block":1002,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"de3a5130a4e170e7c217cec54409f7897a61c4dbc6e95bb58234b4ecfb957b68","quote":"The Company accounts for income taxes in accordance with ASC 740, Income Taxes, using the asset and liability method. Under this method, deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized based on temporary differences between the financial statement carrying amounts and the tax bases of assets and liabilities, using enacted tax rates expected to be in effect in the years in which those temporary differences are expected to reverse. The effect of a change in tax rates on deferred tax assets and liabilities is recognized in income in the period that includes the enactment date.","context":"Income Taxes","section":"Segment Information","block":1004,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"e90dad8d003797a38f6a652bf641a1dfc438df48ceeb26d7c7307ac85789150a","quote":"The Company records a valuation allowance against deferred tax assets to the extent it is more likely than not that some or all of the deferred tax assets will not be realized based on available positive and negative evidence, including future reversals of existing taxable temporary differences, projected future taxable income, and the history of operating losses.","context":"The Company accounts for income taxes in accordance with ASC 740, Income Taxes, using the asset and liability method. Under this method, deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized based on temporary differences between the financial statement carrying amounts and the tax bases of assets and liabilities, using enacted tax rates expected to be in effect in the years in which those temporary differences are expected to reverse. The effect of a change in tax rates on deferred tax assets and liabilities is recognized in income in the period that includes the enactment date.","section":"Segment Information","block":1005,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"b29a0c117df8e3c5e6d9a9fe3e0d99b416950403b785c9bb71c23d5922f95100","quote":"The Company recognizes the tax benefit from an uncertain tax position only if it is more likely than not that the tax position will be sustained upon examination by the relevant taxing authority based on the technical merits of the position. The tax benefit recognized is measured as the largest amount of benefit that has a greater than fifty percent likelihood of being realized upon ultimate settlement. Interest and penalties related to uncertain tax positions, if any, are recognized as a component of income tax expense.","context":"The Company records a valuation allowance against deferred tax assets to the extent it is more likely than not that some or all of the deferred tax assets will not be realized based on available positive and negative evidence, including future reversals of existing taxable temporary differences, projected future taxable income, and the history of operating losses.","section":"Segment Information","block":1006,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-044131","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001843165","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1843165/000121390026044131/ea0281758-10k_lqrhouse.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98.bin","sha256":"93a3cd500156d73a7aef7ef4f9dd199efdeb0a08585ba1e8bd7c7bd1786d6b98"}},{"id":"885d39e621f6424621820fa1f6992eb55bbf99c2b34016bba228219ed7ba03fe","quote":"The Company adopted ASU 2023-09, Improvements to Income Tax Disclosures, for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025. ASU 2023-09 requires enhanced disclosures in the rate reconciliation and additional disaggregation of income taxes paid. The adoption of ASU 2023-09 affected disclosures only and did not have an impact on the Company’s consolidated financial statements.","context":"The Company recognizes the tax benefit from an uncertain tax position only if it is more likely than not that the tax position will be sustained upon examination by the relevant taxing 